---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import ComponentPreview from "../../components/ComponentPreview.astro";

const install = `pnpm add @skryensya/core @skryensya/vanilla`;

const imports = `/* Base: ramps, scale, semantics and state layer. */
@import "@skryensya/core/tokens.scss";

/* Opt-in: Import only the components you ship. */
@import "@skryensya/core/components/button.css";`;

const usage = `<button
  class="sk-button sk-interactive"
  data-sk-button
  data-variant="primary"
>
  Save
</button>
<button
  class="sk-button sk-interactive"
  data-sk-button
  data-variant="neutral"
>
  Cancel
</button>
<button
  class="sk-button sk-interactive"
  data-sk-button
  data-variant="danger"
>
  Delete
</button>`;

const usageReact = `import { Button } from "@skryensya/react/button";

<Button variant="primary">Save</Button>
<Button variant="neutral">Cancel</Button>
<Button variant="danger">Delete</Button>;`;
---

<Base
  title="Installation"
  description="Tokens Sass y componentes: core compartido, vanilla progressive enhancement y React."
>
  <h1>skryensya/ui</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Sass tokens that compile to CSS runtime and components. Tokens still use custom properties, cascade layers and native functions; Components add behavior when the platform does not provide it. If those terms do not sound familiar to you, start with the <a href="/en/prerequisites">prerequisites</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={install} label="terminal" />

  <h2>Importing</h2>
  <p>
    Naked specifiers are resolved by the package's <code>exports</code> map, so you need a bundler (Vite, webpack, Parcel). This site is built exactly like this.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={imports} label="CSS" />

  <h2>Use</h2>
  <p>
    For static components, the class is enough: the CSS brings the structure and its styling hooks. For machined components, <code>@skryensya/vanilla</code> hydrates the authored HTML and <code>@skryensya/react</code> renders the same contract.
  </p>

  <ComponentPreview html={usage} react={usageReact} label="Button" />

  <h2>Components with behavior</h2>
  <p>
    Tabs is already mounted on site as a full vertical slice: <a href="/en/components/tabs">see component</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Try it live</h2>
  <p>
    The controls above change the mode, color palette and contrast. Ramps are configured once from <code>: root</code>, without combinations or brand selectors on disk. Change them and look at the buttons. Then look at the <a class="sk-link sk-interactive" href="/en/reference">token reference</a>, where each resolved value is read back live.
  </p>
</Base>
